  "description": "OTONEU crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H108 N40 O36 Pr9. From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 5 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 5 O neighbors; Pr5 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr6 (Pr) has 5 O neighbors; Pr7 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors; Pr8 (Pr) has 5 O neighbors; Pr9 (Pr) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.963-4.110 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.70-112.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C132H108N40O36Pr9. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
